Does fixed-Q residue covering prove small LRC? Test the (1, lcm(2..Q)) adversary.

n=3 (2 movers): system (1, lcm(2..Qmax)) is blocked at all q<=Qmax, lonely just above:
   Qmax   lcm(2..Qmax)  min lonely q
      8            840             9   (> Qmax: True)
     10           2520            11   (> Qmax: True)
     12          27720            13   (> Qmax: True)
     15         360360            16   (> Qmax: True)
     20      232792560            23   (> Qmax: True)
     25    26771144400            27   (> Qmax: True)
     30  2329089562800            31   (> Qmax: True)

=> minimal lonely denominator grows with the speed (no fixed Q covers all systems).
   The methodology needs a SPEED BOUND to bound Q; then the covering is a finite check.
   (Base reduction 'non-fully-covered => lonely at 1/q' is unaffected and remains proved.)
